The ALFWorld snapshot uses Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct, ALFWorld/TextWorld
training games and the hand-coded ALFWorld expert. Its vendor runtime is
derived from langfengQ/verl-agent commit 20bd331bdbc9026a5668e11362178e10ab7400c8
with local compatibility and fixed-game changes. Upstream notices, licenses
and file hashes are retained in experiments/alfworld/vendor/verl-agent/.
ALFWorld is derived from ALFRED; the underlying games remain attributed to
their upstream authors. Published trajectories add execution records,
next-action supervision and local training/evaluation metadata.

The ALFWorld v0.3.0 model assets derive from Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct,
revision 989aa7980e4cf806f80c7fef2b1adb7bc71aa306 (Apache-2.0). They include
SFT/RL adapters and the preceding training checkpoint, not the full base model.
The inference archive also retains original merged-SFT tensor values at CPU/GPU
rounding differences, allowing exact checkpoint reconstruction on the pinned
software. The original trained adapter tensor bytes remain unchanged.

This repository includes material derived from Gorilla / Berkeley Function
Calling Leaderboard (BFCL), https://github.com/ShishirPatil/gorilla,
commit 6ea57973c7a6097fd7c5915698c54c17c5b1b6c8, licensed under Apache-2.0.
The original license and an exact inventory are in vendor/gorilla/.
The upstream source subset is preserved, including its historical checkout
line endings. Derived data adds executed histories, JSON tool-call messages,
stop replies, fixed split IDs, tokenized targets and audit metadata.

The earlier BFCL E017 adapter is trained from Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B,
revision 70d244cc86ccca08cf5af4e1e306ecf908b1ad5e (Apache-2.0).
Base weights are not included in this repository or the adapter archive.
The adapter configuration replaces its original local model path with the
public model ID and revision; trained tensor bytes are unchanged.

This is an independent project. Upstream names identify data, models and
evaluation methods and do not imply endorsement or affiliation.
